@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] streamed-pose-release
A network proxy stow MUST restore capsule-relative mesh placement even if its bone pose has already
been discarded. Stowing a visual proxy MUST NOT restore local simulation capsule dimensions or position.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] client-skate-sound-selection
Sound-set changes MUST affect only local audio presentation, including remote proxy presentation.
They MUST NOT change simulation, activity/network state, ownership or replicated settings. A fresh
Original selection MUST preserve the legacy load path, references, random state and envelopes.
Invalid or not-ready requests MUST leave current audio unchanged. All replacements MUST be
validated before activation; Original references MUST stay retained for restoration. Changed loops
MUST stop before receiving replacement waves and resume through existing speed, pitch and envelope
logic. Absent override keys MUST inherit Original, never a previous alternative.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] client-skate-audio-preferences
Skate audio preferences MUST affect only local audio presentation, including remote proxy
presentation. At default (no softening, gain one) a request MUST leave loop components, envelopes
and filters untouched. Softening and gain MUST update current and future loops and one-shots for
every sound set, using per-voice filtering and gain, without changing shared waves, envelopes,
pitch, attenuation, timing, simulation or network state. One-shot voices MUST auto-destroy;
EndPlay MUST stop and release only the owned one-shot voices.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] cpu-shading-buffer-lifetime
MeshSurface MUST require actual CPU position and tangent/UV storage before reading render vertices
and normals. Cached raw pointers MUST NOT establish availability after buffer cleanup. When storage
is absent, use the existing cooked-collision surface path and retain material face ownership.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] copied-collision-cache-lifetime
The game-thread mesh-surface cache MUST NOT keep copied triangle arrays for collected mesh UObjects.
The module MUST prune invalid object keys after garbage collection, before replacement assets load,
and remove its callback on shutdown. Pruning MUST drop only cache ownership: active gather jobs retain
immutable shared references, with identical points, normals and material slots until their own release.
Removed cache array bytes MUST be reported separately from actual physical-memory changes; externally
held job data MUST NOT be claimed as reclaimed. Geometry and collision-snapshot semantics stay unchanged.
